    "landing": "4a19761fed343c5aa1659b13af05385221817047",
    "fix": "The landed supervisor RQS custody fix makes the file store name its competing writer: SNAPBACK_REACT_BINDING_RECEIPT_NOT_PERSISTED now carries the competing PID (when known), instance id, lock path, and store path, so a stolen single-writer lock is diagnosable at the refusal instead of by filesystem archaeology. Regression-tested (rqs-store-file suite, same-process and live foreign-writer cases).",
